 the hunter  as craven aaron taylor johnson will be  joined by oscar winner russell crowe in  an unknown familiar role to the hunter  both actors are no stranger to comic  book movies as taylor johnson previously  played quicksilver and avengers age of  ultron whereas crow not only played  superman's biological father and man of  steel but he's also set to appear as  zeus in thor love and thunder later this  year michael mann the acclaimed director  of heat finally has some good news on  this two-decade passion project of his  not only does he have a cast set in  place for his enzo ferrari biopic but he  also has distribution with stx coming on  board  set during the summer of 1957 adam  driver will play enzo ferrari bankruptcy  looms over the company he and his wife  built from nothing 10 years earlier so  he decides to counter his losses by  rolling the dice on one race  one thousand miles across italy birthing  the iconic miley milia penelope cruz and  shailene woodley co-star and man and  crew will finally put rubber to the road  when production starts in italy this may  after spider-man no way home led the box  office for seven of its first eight  weeks of release tom holland is swinging  back into theaters as a young nathan  drake in uncharted  my dude loves swinging uncharted is an  adaptation of the popular adventure  video game series in the film adaptation  tom holland's nathan drake is recruited  by seasoned treasure hunter victor sully  sullivan played by mark wahlberg to  recover a fortune amassed by ferdinand  magellan which was lost 500 years ago if  nate and sully can decipher the clues  and solve one of the world's oldest  mysteries they stand to collect 5  billion dollars worth of treasure but  only if they can learn to work together  fandango correspondent naz perez  recently sat down with holland and  wahlberg to talk about the big action  set pieces particularly one involving  nathan and sully maneuvering around  cargo boxes that tumble out of an  airplane mid-flight i had to train a lot  and i got as strong as i've ever been  but the interesting thing is uh  i basically wanted to put on as much  size as possible you know because next  to mark wahlberg i look like a rake so i  wanted to just get into shape and put on  as much weight as possible but in doing  that you know i didn't do any  cardiovascular  work because i didn't want to burn any  unnecessary calories in the gym meaning  that when we were shooting these long  sequences i was so unfit  like you'd ask me to run a mile and i  would have collapsed so it was tough it  was a sort of double-edged sword of like  i could do pull-ups for days but if you  ask me to run a mile i'd fall apart oh  my god and what was it like shooting it  like did you come out unscathed because  it just looks so  physically intense  i mean there were there were times where  you know we ripped our hands to  smithereens you know like hanging onto  those boxes and eventually your grip  strength would give out and you would  just let go and upon letting go you'd  have rope burn and blisters and bangs  and bruises you know i unfortunately i  kicked a poor stuntman in the face in  that sequence he was okay he is an  ex-ufc fighter so he's tough as nails  that doesn't excuse  my  lack of judgment uh but just the way the  wire work had worked out i was closer to  him than usual and i booted him in the  face but he was okay which was good to  know uh so there's a lot of blood sweat  and tears that went into that sequence  so i was wondering did you get to do  anything in uncharted that you hadn't  done before in a movie um yeah i mean i  probably i've because i've done so much  i've probably done it all but it was the  first time that i just felt like i was  in a big movie like this felt like  indiana jones where you're transported  into a world and you're seeing something  that you're just normally not privy to  seeing that's why it always just felt  like that you know i've done these  little intimate movies i've done many  different kinds of films but this is the  first big like action adventure  blockbuster that takes you on this  magical mystical ride that is full of  adventure and joy it really is like  you're literally on your like at the  edge of your seat until the very end  right after i right after i read i  literally watched every one of the  indiana joneses and then i watched you  know romancing the stone and other  movies that i felt like had some sort of  similarities  this weekend's new theatrical releases  are uncharted and dog heck no no no  no you're just a demon you're just a  demon and dog channing tatum's  directorial debut tatum plays an army  ranger looking to get back into  deployment to show his mental fitness  he's tasked with escorting a trained  military dog named lulu down the pacific  coast in hopes of making it to a fellow  soldier's funeral on time along the way  they drive each other completely crazy  break a handful of laws narrowly evade  death and learn to let down their guards  in order to have a fighting chance of  finding happiness  and available to watch at home this  weekend are parallel mothers and the  king's man  this will not be  a war of heroes  which is all to see  this is going to be fun ray finds stars  in a prequel to the first two kingsman  films the king's man matthew vaughn  continues to mix his adult cocktail of  globetrotting espionage this time with a  dash of the real life mystical figure  rasputin played by rhys iphones gemma  archerton harrison dickinson and jaime  honsu costa amongst the comic violence  that the trilogy is known for  alright well that's it for this week but  before you go let us know which  oscar-nominated movies you need to catch  up on  all right i'm kale and i'll see you next  week i will let you go i promise  we don't pay her enough  [Music]  you

